            <ArticleTitle>Intraforaminal neurinoma in the lumbosacral region.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>86-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A series of 12 patients with intraforaminal neurinomas in the lumbosacral space was reviewed. Our classification according to tumor extension relative to the affected root into intradural intra-arachnoid, intraforaminal extra-arachnoid, and extraforaminal types was useful in determining the best surgical approach to achieve root preservation and minimal postoperative deficits. Where sacrifice of roots was unavoidable, surprisingly few neurological deficits occurred.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
